  "live_records": {
    "q-34572": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34572",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find $q$, if $2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+q[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ q[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ q[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
