    "q-105153": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105153",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find $k$, if $6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 6[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
