    "q-34241": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34241",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find $j$, if ${a}_{1}-j{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $j$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-j{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $j=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
