    "q-105160": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105160",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
