    "q-105158": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105158",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-105158-a",
