    "q-73936": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73936",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find $x$, if $4a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a-2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =4a-b \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(4a-b) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 30 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-73936-a",
