    "q-105163": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105163",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} \\\\ 7{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $(-2)$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1} & =-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+2{x}_{2} & =4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ -(3)+3(-\\frac{11}{2}) & =-11 \\\\ -\\frac{33}{2} & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution.",
