    "q-74028": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74028",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-5 & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means \n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4+(-2)-(-1)=3.\n$$",
