    "q-105172": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105172",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -21{x}_{2} \\\\ -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 0=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-1$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution.",
